@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Fleet local startup and optional GitHub identity
+
+Owner-directed correction: the workbench starts without a ZCode account, occupation questionnaire,
+subscription purchase or cloud configuration gate. The manual preference guide keeps useful local
+settings but loses the vendor artwork and marketing. Existing files and conversation storage stay.
+
+Remove ZCode telemetry/ARMS initialization, cloud rollout fetching, update/forced-upgrade routes,
+commercial account controls and upgrade dialog mounting. Retired product endpoints must fail before
+network I/O even when a stale entry or inherited setting requests them. Model vendor endpoints are
+separate: a user-configured Z.ai/BigModel API key remains a normal optional provider. No default
+ZCode cloud catalog replaces the bundled Fleet templates. Cloud-only functions without a local
+replacement are unavailable, not mocked as successful.
+
+GitHub identity uses the existing Git service and GitHub CLI credential owner (OpenChamber's CLI
+integration is the reference). The footer opens an account menu; explicit login starts `gh auth
+login --web`, presents its device code and reports completion. Account switching/logout operates
+on the selected github.com CLI account, clearly labelled. No copied third-party OAuth client ID,
+new token database, or GitHub requirement for offline work. GitHub repository identity does not
+activate a Copilot subscription; that is a separate model connection.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant UI as Account menu
+  participant Host as Existing Git service
+  participant GH as GitHub CLI / OS credential store
+  UI->>Host: user opens menu / requests login
+  Host->>GH: status / auth login --web
+  GH-->>UI: verification code and status through Host
+  UI->>Host: switch, cancel or disconnect selected account
+  Host->>GH: matching CLI operation only
+```
+
+Acceptance: fresh isolated startup reaches the workbench with no questionnaire or vendor login;
+retired services make zero transport calls (including configured telemetry environments); existing
+API model requests still work under injected fixtures; account operations use argument arrays,
+never return credentials and handle missing CLI/cancel/failure. Actual GitHub authorization is an
+owner action. Visual acceptance covers the original menu/settings patterns in both locales/themes.
+
+GitHub plugin boundary: the footer is optional repository identity, not a complete GitHub plugin.
+OpenAI's public `openai/plugins` repository supplies plugin packaging examples; the installed Codex
+GitHub bundle references an OpenAI-hosted connector plus CLI workflows, whose connector ID is not a
+portable backend. `github/github-mcp-server` and `cli/cli` are the official reusable implementations.
+A future Fleet GitHub package should expose selected tools and native UI contributions through the
+existing plugin/permission host. Do not duplicate tools, copy connector IDs, or equate repository
+authorization with Copilot model access. No GitHub MCP service was installed or activated here.
+
+Offline verification: `pnpm test:fleet-local` covers product-endpoint rejection, no telemetry identity
+or state collection, local help configuration, account projection, missing CLI, cancellation and
+late events, completion/failure and validated account arguments. It does not authorize a real account.
