@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Provider subscriptions and discovery
+
+Fleet extends the existing Provider Settings / Registry / request-auth path. Subscription
+connections are personal provider instances, never the global ZCode login. Each instance owns
+its credentials in the existing CredentialService. No tokens enter provider JSON or renderer.
+
+ChatGPT/Codex and GitHub Copilot authorization use the corresponding pinned Pi OAuth drivers.
+Starting again cancels the old flow. The renderer sees only the verification URL/code and flow
+ID; polling, cancellation, expiration and refresh belong to the host. Disconnect invalidates
+in-flight work before deleting credentials. Refresh is coalesced per connection. Late replies
+cannot restore a disconnected/deleted connection. No paid request is made by login.
+
+A subscription's endpoint/protocol is fixed to its adapter. Before each model request the
+existing runtime-header RPC resolves that connection's credentials; missing credentials fail
+closed. Background/title/compaction requests use the same hook. No vendor gateway rewrites.
+API templates remain editable, independently instantiable, and retain all three native protocols.
+API discovery reads the selected connection's authenticated catalog, imports exact model IDs
+through the existing model mutations and preserves manual overrides. Subscription discovery uses
+the pinned Pi adapter catalog, not a live account entitlement response. Catalog availability is
+not proof of successful inference or entitlement; a model's connection test is a separate action.
+
+UI retains upstream ZCode provider picker, inline editor, model list and feedback patterns.
+Subscription login occupies the API-key section; no extra settings route or app login. The services and adapter packages pin `@earendil-works/pi-ai@0.87.1`; this adds only model transport
+and OAuth drivers, not the Pi Agent execution loop, tools, Session or permission storage. Native Pi
+stream events are converted at the existing model seam. Text, images, tools, reasoning replay and
+cache usage have offline fixtures; unsupported native tools, structured output and raw file inputs
+fail explicitly. Inference uses the existing proxy fetch; OAuth driver networking still follows Pi.
+Live paid inference, actual subscription authorization and owner acceptance remain separate checks.
+
+Kimi Code membership uses its official third-party API-key endpoint, not a copied official-client OAuth identity.
